silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_05_yoneda_for_typed_english_sections_01_representable_as_english_questions_concrete_anchor_3_Hom_X_N#questionsetforx silm:hasLongDescription "The QuestionSetForX is the set of typed-English chains from X to N. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Hom_X_N', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
